---
layout: tutorial
title: Set up Stripe
description: Add paid app subscription plans to your app with Stripe and Appwrite Functions.
step: 2
---

Start by visiting [Stripe](https://stripe.com/) and creating an account. When successful, you will see the Stripe Dashboard.

This tutorial uses a [sandbox](https://docs.stripe.com/sandboxes), Stripe's isolated test environment, so no real money moves. To switch to one, open the account picker in the Dashboard and select **Sandboxes**. The same steps also work in live mode when you're ready to accept real payments.

## API key {% #api-key %}

Open the [API keys](https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys) page while viewing your sandbox. Under **Standard keys**, reveal and copy the **Secret key**, which starts with `sk_test_`. Note it down, as you will need it later when setting the `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` environment variable.

{% only_dark %}
![Stripe API keys page](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/dark/stripe-api-key.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Stripe API keys page](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/stripe-api-key.avif)
{% /only_light %}

## Webhooks {% #webhooks %}

Next, create a webhook so Stripe can notify your function when a subscription starts or ends. You will use a placeholder URL for now in order to get a signing secret. Later, when you set up the Appwrite Function, you will update this webhook with the function's domain.

Open the [Webhooks](https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks) tab in Workbench and click **Add destination**. If you haven't created any destinations yet, the button reads **Create an event destination**. Then, complete the form:

1. If you're asked where to listen for events, select **Your account**.
1. Under the payload format, select **Snapshot**, then leave the **API version** as is.
1. Search for `subscription` and select the `customer.subscription.created` and `customer.subscription.deleted` events. Click **Continue**.
1. Select **Webhook endpoint** as the destination type and click **Continue**.
1. Enter `https://example.com/webhook` as the **Endpoint URL**. Optionally, give the destination a name and description.
1. Click **Create destination**.

{% info title="Select Snapshot, not Thin" %}
Stripe recommends **Thin** events for new integrations, but the template reads the subscription details from each event's payload, which only **Snapshot** events include. With a **Thin** destination, the function can't tell which user subscribed, and the `subscriber` label is never added.
{% /info %}

Once created, Stripe opens the destination's details page. Reveal the **Signing secret**, which starts with `whsec_`, and copy it. Note it down, as you will need it later when setting the `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` environment variable.

{% only_dark %}
![Stripe webhook destination details](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/dark/stripe-webhook-subscription.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Stripe webhook destination details](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/stripe-webhook-subscription.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Keep this page open, as you will need it soon to replace the placeholder URL with your function's domain.
